vout: paused, the subtitles of the picture shown

Paused, the video output drew the subtitles at the pause's date: when the
input took the pause. The pictures it shows until the pause reaches it
(a few ms later) carry later dates and get the subtitles of their dates,
which takes a line that has ended out of the queue. When a line changed
between the two dates, the old line was gone and, at the pause's date, the
next one hadn't begun: the picture paused on showed no line for as long as
it stayed paused (`VLCPausedSubtitleTests`: about one pause in a hundred
just after a line began; the picture right after the pause still had the
line, the ones drawn again while paused none). The subtitles of a paused
picture are those of its own date, as while playing. Applied with patch -p1
(Scripts/build_vlckit_lgpl.sh).

diff --git a/src/video_output/video_output.c b/src/video_output/video_output.c
--- a/src/video_output/video_output.c
+++ b/src/video_output/video_output.c
@@ -987,11 +987,14 @@
      * Get the subpicture to be displayed
      */
     const bool do_snapshot = vout_snapshot_IsRequested(&vout->p->snapshot);
-    vlc_tick_t render_subtitle_date;
-    if (vout->p->pause.is_on)
-        render_subtitle_date = vout->p->pause.date;
-    else
-        render_subtitle_date = filtered->date > 1 ? filtered->date : mdate();
+    /* Changed for Schnellbild on 2026-11-18: Scripts/vlc-patches/0007-vout-paused-the-subtitles-of-the-picture-shown.patch */
+    /* Paused too, the subtitles of the picture's own date: the pause's date
+     * is when the input took the pause, and the pictures the output shows
+     * until the pause reaches it carry later dates; their subtitles, drawn
+     * at their dates, take out a line that ended before them, while at the
+     * pause's date the line after it hasn't begun: the picture paused on
+     * showed none */
+    vlc_tick_t render_subtitle_date = filtered->date > 1 ? filtered->date : mdate();
     vlc_tick_t render_osd_date = mdate(); /* FIXME wrong */
 
